  "dom_id": "step-q101429",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133305/assets/382d511b0797e5b5800bfabc45ab83be7c57439cfe8a4e76da7cfce7f6888661.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of circles to pentagons?",
  "worked_solution": "We can express the ratio of the number of circles to the number of pentagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of circles}:\\text{number of pentagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of circles. There are $2$ circles.\n\n- Next, we count the number of pentagons. There are $2$ pentagons.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of circles to pentagons is $2:2.$",
